+# Destructive Bash command guard
+
+A Claude Code `PreToolUse` hook that blocks the bounty's five destructive command classes before the Bash tool executes. It logs each block as JSONL to `~/.claude/hooks/blocked.log` with UTC timestamp, command, project path, and reasons.
+
+## Install — two commands
+
+```bash
+mkdir -p ~/.claude/hooks && cp block_destructive_commands.py ~/.claude/hooks/
+python - <<'PY'
+import json, pathlib
+p=pathlib.Path.home()/'.claude/settings.json'; p.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
+d=json.loads(p.read_text()) if p.exists() else {}
+d.setdefault('hooks',{})['PreToolUse']=[{'matcher':'Bash','hooks':[{'type':'command','command':'python3 ~/.claude/hooks/block_destructive_commands.py'}]}]
+p.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\n')
+PY
+```
+
+Claude Code sends the hook event on stdin. A blocked command emits a clear reason on stderr and exits `2`, the documented blocking exit code for `PreToolUse` command hooks.
+
+## Guarded patterns
+
+- recursive forced removal: `rm -rf` and equivalent `rm -fr`
+- `DROP TABLE`
+- `git push --force` / `git push -f`
+- `TRUNCATE`
+- `DELETE FROM ...` without a `WHERE` clause in the same SQL statement
+
+This is a focused guard, **not a general shell sandbox**. It intentionally leaves ordinary Bash commands untouched.
+
+## Test
+
+```bash
+python -m unittest -v test_block_destructive_commands.py
+```
